# Close-out E1: a settle and a release of one reserve race on one (user, module) and the reserve is never spent twice. The fault removes BOTH protections (the store's advisory lock becomes a no-op SELECT, and the per-reserve CHECK reserves_not_overspent becomes `OR true`): with the test holding the balance row, the settle is in flight when the release starts, the release reads the whole remainder, both commit, and the reserve is charged 6 and released 10 against 10. The invariant checker must say so before anything else.
GATE=interleave-settle-release
TARGET=platform
SETUP=
STEP=go test TestCloseoutMoney_SettleVsRelease_InterleavedAtTheBalanceWrite (database integration test, real Postgres)
CMD=H_PG_ADMIN_DSN="$FAULT_ADMIN_DSN" bash tests/harness/run-db-tests.sh '^TestCloseoutMoney_SettleVsRelease_InterleavedAtTheBalanceWrite$'
MESSAGE=--- FAIL: TestCloseoutMoney_SettleVsRelease_InterleavedAtTheBalanceWrite
MESSAGE=MONEY INVARIANT VIOLATED
MESSAGE=platform.reserve_overdrawn has a row
